            "text": "```python\nimport numpy as np\n\n\ndef main():\n    # Load the array without modifying the file\n    vectors = np.load(\"vectors.npy\")\n\n    # Cast to float64 to ensure high numerical precision\n    X = vectors.astype(np.float64)\n    n = X.shape[0]\n\n    # Precompute squared L2 norms of each row\n    sq_norms = np.sum(X**2, axis=1)\n\n    total_distance = 0.0\n    chunk_size = 1000\n\n    # Process in chunks to maintain low memory usage while utilizing optimized BLAS GEMM\n    for i in range(0, n, chunk_size):\n        end = min(i + chunk_size, n)\n\n        # Compute dot products for the current chunk against all vectors\n        gram_chunk = np.dot(X[i:end], X.T)\n\n        # ||u - v||^2 = ||u||^2 + ||v||^2 - 2 * <u, v>\n        d_sq = sq_norms[i:end, np.newaxis] + sq_norms[np.newaxis, :] - 2.0 * gram_chunk\n        np.maximum(d_sq, 0.0, out=d_sq)\n\n        # Explicitly ensure exact self-distance diagonal is zero\n        for row_idx in range(i, end):\n            d_sq[row_idx - i, row_idx] = 0.0\n\n        distances = np.sqrt(d_sq)\n        total_distance += np.sum(distances)\n\n    print(f\"TOTAL:{total_distance}\")\n\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    main()\n```",
